is just good.

19:38.000 --> 19:41.000
I think it's something that is
worth looking at.

19:41.000 --> 19:45.000
This is an audio blog post
titled Toys or Tools.

19:45.000 --> 19:46.000
One of the consumers.

19:46.500 --> 19:52.500
The most consistent themes
that's come up in my recent
conversations with photographers
about their equipment choices

19:52.500 --> 19:58.500
is the challenge that they have
in taking digital photography
seriously.

19:58.500 --> 20:05.500
Admittedly, because of my
personal history in photography,
a lot of my friends are large
format photographers.

20:05.500 --> 20:08.500
They're shooting 4x5s and 8x10
cameras.

20:08.500 --> 20:12.500
And these are cameras that it's
pretty easy to take seriously.

20:12.500 --> 20:17.500
They're expensive, there's a lot
of gadgets that have to be
employed in order to use them
successfully.

20:17.500 --> 20:20.500
It's expensive to shoot sheet
film, etc.

20:20.500 --> 20:27.500
And somehow when these people
pick up a digital camera, it
just feels like a toy to them.

20:27.500 --> 20:34.500
Everything is automatic, focus
is automatic, exposure is
automatic, bracketing is
automatic.

20:34.500 --> 20:38.500
There's no film costs. They
don't have to develop the film
when they get home.

20:38.500 --> 20:41.500
It just doesn't feel like a
serious tool.

20:41.500 --> 20:47.500
But yet, those people who are
using these tools in a serious
way are realizing that...

20:48.000 --> 20:50.000
that they can do some very nice
photographs

20:50.000 --> 20:52.000
and some really interesting
artwork.

20:54.000 --> 21:00.000
That leads me to think that when
it comes to tools, it's not the
nature of the tool

21:00.000 --> 21:03.000
that determines whether or not
it's a serious tool.

21:03.000 --> 21:06.000
It's the nature of the
photographer's mind.

21:06.000 --> 21:12.000
If we approach the use of a tool
in a serious way, if we approach
it with a certain amount

21:12.000 --> 21:21.000
of creativity, reverence,
respect for what it can do, then
it can be a serious tool.

21:21.000 --> 21:27.000
But if you insist that a toy is
merely a toy and you don't
approach it carefully

21:27.000 --> 21:35.000
and thoughtfully and
deliberately, then a toy will be
a toy and the results will be
likewise.

21:35.000 --> 21:42.000
So that's something that all,
everyone who works at a big
co-publisher or media company

21:42.000 --> 21:47.000
should listen to that at least
twice a day.

21:47.000 --> 21:53.000
Because yeah, it's about the
effort you put into these toys,
but we're doing a lot of cool
stuff.

21:53.000 --> 21:55.000
